WEBVTT

00:00:10.432 --> 00:00:12.375
Cambridge English Readers.

00:00:12.434 --> 00:00:14.438
Starter Level.

00:00:14.498 --> 00:00:18.883
The Black Pearls by Richard McCandrew.

00:00:18.944 --> 00:00:22.488
Published by Cambridge University Press.

00:00:22.548 --> 00:00:32.617
This recording is copyright.

00:00:32.677 --> 00:00:59.181
The Black Pearls by Richard McCandrew Chapter 1 Who is Wolfgang Peters?

00:00:59.241 --> 00:01:06.909
This is the man, says Janet Hunter, and she puts a photo on the table.

00:01:06.969 --> 00:01:11.871
Janet Hunter is a police inspector from New Zealand.

00:01:11.931 --> 00:01:20.034
She's in the police station on Rauratonga, one of the Cook Islands in the Pacific Ocean.

00:01:20.094 --> 00:01:22.364
What's his name?

00:01:22.424 --> 00:01:25.456
Asks to Nui Epati.

00:01:25.516 --> 00:01:31.130
Eppati is an inspector in the Cook Islands Police.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:36.572
His name is Wolfgang Peters, she answers.

00:01:36.632 --> 00:01:41.004
Some people call him the minute man.

00:01:41.063 --> 00:01:42.224
Why?

00:01:42.244 --> 00:01:44.816
Eppati asks.

00:01:44.876 --> 00:01:52.809
Because one minute he's there, and the next minute he's not, answers Hunter.

00:01:52.869 --> 00:01:56.136
Eppati smiles.

00:01:56.196 --> 00:01:59.844
And why do you want him?"

00:01:59.904 --> 00:02:01.944
Apati asks.

00:02:02.004 --> 00:02:04.536
He looks at the photo.

00:02:04.596 --> 00:02:08.446
He steals, answers Hunter.

00:02:08.506 --> 00:02:13.108
He takes things, often from museums.

00:02:13.168 --> 00:02:16.109
People tell him what they want.

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:19.220
Then he steals for them.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:23.398
And he gets very good money for his work.

00:02:23.458 --> 00:02:26.878
What kind of things does he take?

00:02:26.938 --> 00:02:29.200
asks a patty.

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:32.432
Anything, answers Hunter.

00:02:32.492 --> 00:02:37.868
A Faberge egg from a museum in Virginia, in the United States.

00:02:37.927 --> 00:02:43.792
A Picasso painting from a museum in St. Petersburg, in Russia.

00:02:43.852 --> 00:02:50.748
And then this year, an old book from a museum in Auckland, in New Zealand.

00:02:50.808 --> 00:02:53.954
It's the only one in the world.

00:02:54.014 --> 00:02:57.322
That's why I'm after him.

00:02:57.382 --> 00:03:01.637
I see, says Eppati.

00:03:01.697 --> 00:03:06.074
Peter's is very good, says Hunter.

00:03:06.134 --> 00:03:11.324
But I want him, and I'm going to get him.

00:03:11.384 --> 00:03:14.260
And he's coming here?

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:16.372
Do Rada Tonga?

00:03:16.432 --> 00:03:18.422
asks Epati.

00:03:18.482 --> 00:03:21.094
Yes, says Hunter.

00:03:21.154 --> 00:03:28.030
We, the New Zealand police, think he's going to steal something here.

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:31.672
Ah, says Epati.

00:03:31.732 --> 00:03:36.226
Then I know what, I think.

00:03:36.286 --> 00:03:40.801
Apati takes down a book and opens it.

00:03:40.861 --> 00:03:43.224
Hunter watches him.

00:03:43.284 --> 00:03:47.388
Many Cook Islanders are big people.

00:03:47.448 --> 00:03:50.691
Apati is big.

00:03:50.751 --> 00:03:53.464
He gives Hunter the book.

00:03:53.524 --> 00:04:00.180
It's open at a photo of a beautiful necklace of black pearls.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:06.616
That is the Manihiki necklace, says Epati.

00:04:06.676 --> 00:04:10.760
It's from the island of Manihiki.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:19.929
Manihiki is a thousand kilometers from Ratonga, but it's one of the Cook Islands too.

00:04:19.989 --> 00:04:23.217
Hunter looks at the necklace.

00:04:23.277 --> 00:04:27.415
It's beautiful, she says.

00:04:27.474 --> 00:04:31.176
Yes, says Epati.

00:04:31.236 --> 00:04:38.601
And over a hundred years old, those are black pearls.

00:04:38.661 --> 00:04:41.372
They're not easy to find.

00:04:41.432 --> 00:04:47.256
You only get them in Tahiti and here in the Cook Islands.

00:04:47.316 --> 00:04:50.796
Hunter looks up at Epati.

00:04:50.856 --> 00:04:57.698
The necklace is in the museum here, says Epati.

00:04:57.758 --> 00:05:02.292
People from all over the world come to see it.

00:05:02.352 --> 00:05:06.516
He takes the photo of Peters from the table.

00:05:06.576 --> 00:05:09.249
Can I have this photo?

00:05:09.308 --> 00:05:10.810
He asks.

00:05:10.869 --> 00:05:14.432
Of course, answers Hunter.

00:05:14.492 --> 00:05:22.436
Then she says, Peter's is coming here this morning on a plane from Tahiti.

00:05:22.496 --> 00:05:26.390
I want to watch him and try and get him.

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:29.252
But is that okay with you?

00:05:29.312 --> 00:05:32.966
After all, this is your island.

00:05:33.025 --> 00:05:36.278
That's okay, says Epati.

00:05:36.338 --> 00:05:38.550
Do you want any help?

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:42.726
We have some good people in the Cook Islands police.

00:05:42.786 --> 00:05:46.870
Thank you, says Hunter, but not now.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:48.751
I can call you.

00:05:48.811 --> 00:05:52.252
Of course, says Apati.

00:05:52.312 --> 00:05:55.284
Call me by five o'clock.

00:05:55.344 --> 00:05:58.105
Okay, says Hunter.

00:05:58.164 --> 00:06:01.276
They go out of the police station.

00:06:01.335 --> 00:06:04.096
Which hotel are you in?

00:06:04.156 --> 00:06:06.338
asks Apati.

00:06:06.398 --> 00:06:08.350
The water side in?

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:10.194
Answers, Hunter.

00:06:10.254 --> 00:06:14.178
Good hotel, says Epati.

00:06:14.238 --> 00:06:18.030
Is this your first time in the Cook Islands?

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:20.963
Yes, says Hunter.

00:06:21.022 --> 00:06:24.056
It's very beautiful here.

00:06:24.116 --> 00:06:27.658
Well, thank you for your help, Inspector.

00:06:27.718 --> 00:06:33.433
I must get to the airport by eleven o'clock.

00:06:33.493 --> 00:06:40.766
Chapter 2 watching Peters.

00:06:40.826 --> 00:06:45.768
A lot of people are waiting in front of the airport.

00:06:45.828 --> 00:06:50.790
What are all these people doing thinks Hunter?

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:56.273
She walks across and speaks to a Cook Islands woman.

00:06:56.332 --> 00:06:58.684
Why is everyone here?

00:06:58.744 --> 00:07:02.426
She asks, Kate Watson is coming.

00:07:02.485 --> 00:07:07.903
The woman answers, you know, the Kate Watson.

00:07:07.963 --> 00:07:11.690
She's in a lot of Hollywood films.

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:15.574
Oh, her, says Hunter.

00:07:15.633 --> 00:07:18.536
Is she making a film here?

00:07:18.596 --> 00:07:19.876
She asks.

00:07:19.936 --> 00:07:26.462
Yes, but she's only on the island for two or three days.

00:07:26.522 --> 00:07:31.096
Hunter waits next to the woman for a minute or two.

00:07:31.156 --> 00:07:34.636
Then she goes to her car.

00:07:34.696 --> 00:07:42.047
At about 1145, Wolfgang Peters comes out of the airport.

00:07:42.107 --> 00:07:46.179
He's a short man with dark hair.

00:07:46.238 --> 00:07:49.450
Hunter watches from her car.

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:54.081
Peters finds a taxi and gets in.

00:07:54.141 --> 00:07:57.162
The taxi drives away.

00:07:57.222 --> 00:08:00.816
Hunter drives behind it.

00:08:00.876 --> 00:08:11.466
After 15 minutes, the taxi stops at the water side in, and Peter's gets out with his bags.

00:08:11.526 --> 00:08:15.398
That's good, thinks Hunter.

00:08:15.458 --> 00:08:18.410
He's at this hotel too.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:21.492
It's going to be easy to watch him.

00:08:21.552 --> 00:08:27.245
She sits in her car across the street and waits.

00:08:27.305 --> 00:08:32.036
At 1.30, Peters comes out of the hotel.

00:08:32.056 --> 00:08:35.257
Our taxi is waiting.

00:08:35.318 --> 00:08:40.390
Peters gets in and the taxi drives away.

00:08:40.451 --> 00:08:44.302
Hunter is behind them.

00:08:44.362 --> 00:08:49.256
Peters taxi takes him to the museum.

00:08:49.316 --> 00:08:54.089
He gets out and walks into the museum.

00:08:54.148 --> 00:08:59.632
Hunter leaves her car and goes in too.

00:08:59.692 --> 00:09:02.944
The museum is small.

00:09:03.004 --> 00:09:12.056
There are a lot of interesting things from the Cook Islands and from Tahiti, Tonga and Fiji.

00:09:12.116 --> 00:09:21.120
Hunter looks at some old bags and jackets from the Cook Islands, but she watches Peter's too.

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:26.082
He's looking at the money he can necklace.

00:09:26.142 --> 00:09:30.915
After a minute or two, he looks across the room.

00:09:30.975 --> 00:09:36.839
Hunter turns and walks over to a boat from the time of Captain Cook.

00:09:36.898 --> 00:09:40.289
She doesn't want Peter's to see her.

00:09:40.349 --> 00:09:43.988
Peter's looks at the necklace again.

00:09:44.048 --> 00:09:47.760
Then he leaves the museum.

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:50.920
Hunter waits five minutes.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:58.052
Then she too leaves and goes to the water side in.

00:09:58.112 --> 00:10:03.713
Chapter 3 At C.J.'

00:10:03.693 --> 00:10:09.774
's Cafe Peter's is here, says Hunter.

00:10:09.834 --> 00:10:12.508
It's six o'clock in the evening.

00:10:12.568 --> 00:10:17.661
She's sitting with Tunui Epati at CJ's cafe.

00:10:17.722 --> 00:10:20.704
They're looking out over the water.

00:10:20.764 --> 00:10:26.119
And he is going to steal the money he can necklace.

00:10:26.179 --> 00:10:31.910
Well, says Epati, we can stop him.

00:10:31.969 --> 00:10:42.073
I can get some police officers to watch the necklace all the time, or we can try and get him with the necklace.

00:10:42.133 --> 00:10:49.528
I want to get him with the necklace, says Hunter, but it's not going to be easy.

00:10:49.589 --> 00:10:53.022
He is very good at his job.

00:10:53.082 --> 00:11:02.062
I can put some police officers in the museum, says Epati, where Peters can't see them.

00:11:02.122 --> 00:11:11.021
You can, says Hunter, but they're not going to get him, asks Epatty.

00:11:11.081 --> 00:11:13.402
Hunter smiles.

00:11:13.462 --> 00:11:17.556
The police never do, she says.

00:11:17.616 --> 00:11:21.138
Well, says Epatty.

00:11:21.198 --> 00:11:23.910
He's at the water side in.

00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:27.934
We can look for the necklace in his room.

00:11:27.994 --> 00:11:36.638
You can try looking in his room too, says Hunter, but he never has the things with him.

00:11:36.698 --> 00:11:46.869
Virginia, St. Petersburg, Auckland, the police never find anything, but she stops and thinks.

00:11:46.929 --> 00:11:51.958
He has a plane ticket to Tahiti the day after tomorrow.

00:11:52.018 --> 00:11:56.340
And he's not going to leave the necklace here in Raritonga.

00:11:56.401 --> 00:11:59.522
No, Apati says.

00:11:59.582 --> 00:12:02.774
Peter's isn't working for a Cook Islander.

00:12:02.834 --> 00:12:05.676
No one here has that much money.

00:12:05.736 --> 00:12:10.169
Peter's is going to have the necklace with him at the airport.

00:12:10.229 --> 00:12:12.722
We can get him there.

00:12:12.782 --> 00:12:16.566
And no police officers in the museum?

00:12:16.626 --> 00:12:18.256
Ask Hunter?

00:12:18.316 --> 00:12:19.637
No.

00:12:19.697 --> 00:12:22.278
Says Epatty.

00:12:22.338 --> 00:12:27.449
Epatty and Hunter leave CJ's cafe.

00:12:27.509 --> 00:12:34.861
Across the street, a lot of people are waiting in front of the Itutaki restaurant.

00:12:34.921 --> 00:12:38.035
Some police officers are there too.

00:12:38.095 --> 00:12:43.029
A car drives up and two women get out.

00:12:43.089 --> 00:12:48.730
The first has long red hair and is very beautiful.

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:53.141
Hunter knows her face from films and papers.

00:12:53.201 --> 00:12:56.242
People shout, Kate!

00:12:56.302 --> 00:12:57.662
Kate!

00:12:57.722 --> 00:12:59.932
How are you, Kate?

00:12:59.992 --> 00:13:03.240
Do you like Raritonga, Kate?

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:06.548
The second woman has dark hair.

00:13:06.608 --> 00:13:08.878
She's beautiful too.

00:13:08.938 --> 00:13:11.709
Hunter looks at apathy.

00:13:11.769 --> 00:13:14.619
Who's the woman with dark hair?

00:13:14.679 --> 00:13:16.210
She asks.

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:20.471
Maria Gomez answers apathy.

00:13:20.531 --> 00:13:24.082
She's in the Kate Watson film too.

00:13:24.142 --> 00:13:31.015
She's not famous now, but people say she's the next big thing.

00:13:31.075 --> 00:13:35.840
the women's smile and go into the restaurant.

00:13:35.900 --> 00:13:38.982
Apati looks at Hunter.

00:13:39.042 --> 00:13:45.236
Hollywood comes to Raradonga, he says, with a small smile.

00:13:45.296 --> 00:13:50.399
It's all work for me.

00:13:50.459 --> 00:13:58.172
Chapter 4 Who takes the necklace?

00:13:58.232 --> 00:14:04.004
At nine o'clock the next morning, the museum is opening.

00:14:04.064 --> 00:14:07.466
Hunter is sitting in her car.

00:14:07.526 --> 00:14:11.420
She's watching the front door of the museum.

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:17.724
After five minutes, Apaty comes out and walks across to her.

00:14:17.784 --> 00:14:23.057
The people at the museum understand, says Apaty.

00:14:23.117 --> 00:14:28.299
They know about Peters, and they're not going to try and stop him.

00:14:28.359 --> 00:14:31.270
Okay, says Hunter.

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:34.521
Well, says Apaty.

00:14:34.581 --> 00:14:36.232
I'm leaving.

00:14:36.292 --> 00:14:40.464
We don't want Peters to see any police officers here.

00:14:40.524 --> 00:14:42.815
And I've got work to do.

00:14:42.876 --> 00:14:45.618
What are you going to do?

00:14:45.678 --> 00:14:51.931
I'm just going to wait here in the car for now and watch, says Hunter.

00:14:51.991 --> 00:14:53.652
Okay.

00:14:53.712 --> 00:14:57.864
Apaty gets in his car and drives away.

00:14:57.924 --> 00:15:02.634
People come and go in and out of the museum.

00:15:02.695 --> 00:15:12.728
Then, at about 1130, a taxi drives up and a woman with long dark hair gets out.

00:15:12.788 --> 00:15:15.679
She has a bag in one hand.

00:15:15.739 --> 00:15:21.471
She looks at Hunter's car and then walks into the museum fast.

00:15:21.531 --> 00:15:24.652
Hunter watches the woman.

00:15:24.712 --> 00:15:27.931
Something's wrong, she thinks.

00:15:27.991 --> 00:15:31.010
I don't think that's a woman."

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:33.743
She gets out of her car fast.

00:15:33.802 --> 00:15:37.685
There's a noise from the museum and a lot of shouting.

00:15:37.745 --> 00:15:43.849
She runs to the museum, but people are running out with their hands over their faces.

00:15:43.909 --> 00:15:47.311
Hunter tries to get in, but she can't.

00:15:47.371 --> 00:15:49.432
She runs to the back door.

00:15:49.492 --> 00:15:50.793
It's open.

00:15:50.853 --> 00:15:53.848
Two people from the museum come out.

00:15:53.908 --> 00:15:56.851
The necklace shouts one.

00:15:56.911 --> 00:16:01.372
It's not there!

00:16:01.432 --> 00:16:05.633
Chapter 5.

00:16:05.693 --> 00:16:09.334
Peters knows nothing.

00:16:09.394 --> 00:16:14.075
The minute man says a patty.

00:16:14.135 --> 00:16:16.986
Yes, says Hunter.

00:16:17.046 --> 00:16:20.647
There one minute, not the next.

00:16:20.707 --> 00:16:24.845
Or this time, he's the minute woman.

00:16:24.905 --> 00:16:32.816
It's six o'clock in the evening and they're drinking coconut water at the water side in.

00:16:32.876 --> 00:16:35.778
What does Peter's say?

00:16:35.838 --> 00:16:37.299
asks Hunter?

00:16:37.359 --> 00:16:38.570
Nothing.

00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:40.581
Answers a patty.

00:16:40.641 --> 00:16:46.684
Three hours of questions this afternoon and no answers from him.

00:16:46.744 --> 00:16:51.636
He's not the woman at the museum, asks Hunter.

00:16:51.696 --> 00:16:55.768
Her mouth smiles, but not her eyes.

00:16:55.828 --> 00:16:59.749
He says not, says Apati.

00:16:59.809 --> 00:17:02.700
Of course, says Hunter.

00:17:02.760 --> 00:17:05.730
And what about his room here?

00:17:05.791 --> 00:17:09.562
No necklace, says Apati.

00:17:09.622 --> 00:17:13.990
No long dark hair, nothing.

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:17.580
Then why is he in Raritonga?

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:19.031
asks Hunter.

00:17:19.090 --> 00:17:21.462
She smiles again.

00:17:21.522 --> 00:17:25.835
He says he's just enjoying our beautiful island.

00:17:25.895 --> 00:17:27.526
Says Epatty.

00:17:27.586 --> 00:17:32.059
Lots of good food and friendly people.

00:17:32.119 --> 00:17:34.260
Where is he now?

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:35.842
asks Hunter.

00:17:35.902 --> 00:17:40.964
Here, in the restaurant, eating and drinking.

00:17:41.024 --> 00:17:43.145
Epatty laughs.

00:17:43.205 --> 00:17:48.926
And this evening, there's some Cook Islands dancing at the hotel.

00:17:48.986 --> 00:17:55.617
He's going to watch that, because he tells me he loves dancing.

00:17:55.678 --> 00:17:59.429
He's good, says Hunter.

00:17:59.489 --> 00:18:03.700
Very good, says Epati.

00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:06.801
Epati looks at Hunter.

00:18:06.861 --> 00:18:09.402
Do you like dancing?

00:18:09.462 --> 00:18:11.015
He asks.

00:18:11.075 --> 00:18:14.530
I do now, she answers.

00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:17.934
I want to watch Peters.

00:18:17.994 --> 00:18:24.339
At nine o'clock, Hunter leaves her room and goes down to the restaurant.

00:18:24.400 --> 00:18:27.983
She hears a lot of noise and shouting.

00:18:28.043 --> 00:18:29.434
Cade!

00:18:29.494 --> 00:18:30.475
Cade!

00:18:30.535 --> 00:18:32.848
Are you here for the dancing?

00:18:32.908 --> 00:18:36.494
Do you like Cook Island's dancing?

00:18:36.554 --> 00:18:40.410
Kate Watson comes into the hotel.

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:43.330
Maria Gomez is with her.

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:47.471
Hunter walks into the restaurant behind them.

00:18:47.532 --> 00:18:53.954
In the restaurant, Kate Watson and Maria Gomez sit at the front.

00:18:54.014 --> 00:18:57.014
Hunter looks for Peters.

00:18:57.074 --> 00:19:01.496
He is sitting behind Kate Watson.

00:19:01.556 --> 00:19:04.221
The dancing starts.

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:10.498
Men, women, boys and girls, all with flowers in their hair.

00:19:10.558 --> 00:19:14.410
Beautiful dances to beautiful music.

00:19:14.470 --> 00:19:17.132
Everyone enjoys it.

00:19:17.192 --> 00:19:23.535
The dancing finishes at 10.30 and everyone gets up to leave.

00:19:23.595 --> 00:19:30.248
People go to the restaurant doors, hunter waits and watches.

00:19:30.308 --> 00:19:36.784
Peters speaks to one or two people Then he goes to the doors.

00:19:36.844 --> 00:19:40.194
Watson and Gomez are leaving too.

00:19:40.254 --> 00:19:43.346
Hunter can just see their heads.

00:19:43.406 --> 00:19:46.506
Peters is just in front of them.

00:19:46.566 --> 00:19:49.727
Kate Watson says something to him.

00:19:49.787 --> 00:19:54.848
He turns and smiles, but says nothing.

00:19:54.908 --> 00:20:00.890
People out on the street are shouting, Kate, Kate!

00:20:00.950 --> 00:20:03.922
Hunter watches Peters.

00:20:03.982 --> 00:20:07.194
He turns left to his room.

00:20:07.254 --> 00:20:16.572
Kate Watson and Maria Gomez go out of the hotel and get into a car.

00:20:16.632 --> 00:20:20.866
Chapter 6.

00:20:20.926 --> 00:20:23.757
At the airport.

00:20:23.817 --> 00:20:31.296
It's 10 o'clock in the morning, and Hunter and Aparti are at the airport.

00:20:31.356 --> 00:20:34.040
They're watching people.

00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:37.211
Two planes are leaving this morning.

00:20:37.271 --> 00:20:41.702
